{{Quote|Come on, come on, come on, come on!|Vangos Grek|audio=Grek-ComeOn.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
'''Vangos Grek''' was a [[human]] [[Rebel pilot|pilot]] who served in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. He was stationed at the [[Tierfon Launch Base|launch base]] on the [[planet]] [[Tierfon]] and flew as part of the [[Tierfon Yellow Aces]] until the base was scuttled and the [[squadron]] broken up due to increasing [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] activity. Grek and three other [[pilot]]s from the squadron were reassigned to the Alliance's [[Great Temple]] headquarters on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]].

Grek was made a part of [[Blue Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Blue Squadron]] and flew under the [[Blue Six]] [[callsign]] during the [[Battle of Scarif]] in [[1 BBY]]. When Blue Squadron was ordered to support [[Rogue One|Alliance forces]] on the surface of the planet [[Scarif]], Grek raced to make it through the planet's [[Shield Gate]] before it could close; however, he lagged behind and was [[Death|killed]] when he crashed his [[T-65 X-wing starfighter]] into the gate after it had shut.

==Biography==
===Yellow Ace===
{{Quote|Blue Squadron, get to the surface before they close that gate.|Raddus|audio=Raddus-BlueSquadron.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:TierfonYellowAces.svg|thumb|left|300px|Vangos Grek flew as one of the Tierfon Yellow Aces.]]
The [[human]]<ref name="Rogue One" /> Vangos Grek served as a [[Rebel pilot|pilot]] in the [[Rebel Alliance Starfighter Corps|Starfighter Corps]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="HC79" /> He<ref name="ROJN" /> became a part of the [[Tierfon Yellow Aces]], a [[squadron]] based out of the [[Tierfon Launch Base|rebel launch base]] on the<ref name="HC79" /> [[Expansion Region]]<ref name="RebelFiles">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> [[planet]] [[Tierfon]]. The squadron flew sortie after sortie from the base until their successes led to increased [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] activity in the [[sector]].<ref name="HC79" /> Encroaching Imperial patrols forced the Alliance to scuttle the base and the Aces squadron was broken apart and reassigned to other outposts. Grek was moved to the Alliance's headquarters in the [[Great Temple]] on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]] alongside fellow Yellow Aces [[Zal Dinnes]], [[Jek Tono Porkins]],<ref name="UVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> and [[Robich Duggsin]];<ref name="HC79" /> the largest contingent of [[pilot]]s from the squadron to be assigned to the same location.<ref name="UVG" />

Grek and Duggsin became part of [[Blue Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Blue Squadron]] under the [[Commanding officer|command]] of [[General]] [[Antoc Merrick]], while Dinnes and Porkins joined [[Red Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Red Squadron]].<ref name="UVG" /> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> Blue Squadron was among the [[Alliance Military|forces]] scrambled by [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] to aid a [[Rogue One|group of rebels]] attempting to [[Battle of Scarif|steal]] the [[Death Star plans|plans]] to the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]] on the planet [[Scarif]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> With Grek flying a [[T-65 X-wing starfighter]] under the [[callsign]] [[Blue Six]],<ref name="UVG" /> the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]] dropped out of [[hyperspace]] in the [[Scarif system]] and engaged the [[Imperial Navy|Imperial forces]] stationed there. Raddus gave the order for Blue Squadron to support the [[Alliance Army|ground forces]] during the battle, meaning the squadron would need to pass through the Imperial [[Shield Gate]] that acted as the only entry point through Scarif's [[planetary shield]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

===Race for the gate===
{{Quote|Pull up!''"<br />[Grek screams]|quoteend=0|Barion Raner tries to save Vangos Grek|audio=Raner-Grek.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:VangosGrekDeath-RO.png|thumb|right|300px|Vangos Grek was killed when he crashed into the Scarif Shield Gate.]]
Merrick gave the order for the squadron to form up on him, and the pilots began racing through the [[Golan M3185 space station|gate]] before it could be shut.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Grek and<ref name="ROJN" /> [[Barion Raner]],<ref name="UVG" /> flying as [[Blue Four]], lagged behind some of the other pilots<ref name="ROJN" /> as part of a second wave,<ref name="RON">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref> but were determined to make it through; however, as Grek shouted at he and Raner's [[engine]]s to speed up, Raner realized they were not going to make it. Pulling up, he called a warning to Grek over comms,<ref name="ROJN" /> but Blue Six kept going and, alongside another pilot, he crashed into the [[Space station|gate]], which had finished closing.<ref name="Rogue One" />

The first [[fleet]] casualty of the battle,<ref name="RON" /> Grek was [[Death|killed]] as his vehicle exploded into a bright ball of [[fire]], leaving Merrick to wonder if the pilot had kept his X-wing at full speed the entire [[time]] or whether another [[Standard second|second]] of acceleration might have made a difference.<ref name="ROJN" /> The Alliance ultimately managed to steal the plans during the battle, but all members of Blue Squadron who had made it through the gate before Grek, including Merrick, also perished.<ref name="HC71">{{HelmetCollectionCite|71|Weapons & Uniforms}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
Grek urged his vehicle to hurry while trying to make it through the gate, but then screamed as he realized he was going to crash. He had light skin.<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Equipment==
Grek's [[K-22995 light flight helmet]] was gray and red and bore two of the bright yellow [[Starbird (symbol)|starbirds]] of the Tierfon Yellow Aces,<ref name="UVG" /> which were common among those who had served at Tierfon.<ref name="HC79" /> He also wore a blue [[flight suit]] with a white [[flight harness]] and a gray [[Diagnostech life support unit]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Grek_helmet.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Vangos Grek's [[flight helmet]]]]
Vangos Grek was created for the ''[[Star Wars Anthology Series]]'' film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Rogue One" /> which was released on [[December 16]], [[2016]].<ref name="ReleaseDate">{{SW|url=news/gareth-edwards-and-gary-whitta-onboard-for-star-wars-stand-alone-film|text=Gareth Edwards and Gary Whitta Onboard for ''Star Wars'' Stand-Alone Film}}</ref> The character was first revealed in the second trailer for the film on [[October 13]] of that year.<ref name="Trailer 2">{{SWYouTube|sC9abcLLQpI|Rogue One: A Star Wars Story Trailer #2 (Official)|sw_url=video/rogue-one-a-star-wars-story-trailer-2}}</ref> Grek was not identified in the film,<ref name="Rogue One" /> but the accompanying [[Star Wars: Rogue One: A Junior Novel|junior novelization]] by [[Matt Forbeck]] identified the character by the callsign Blue Six.<ref name="ROJN" />

The accompanying reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]], identified Blue Six as Vangos Grek as part of the label for an image of the helmet worn by Grek.<ref name="UVG" /> A separate unnamed pilot wearing the same helmet is mislabeled as Grek in the [[2017]] reference book ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story - The Official Mission Debrief]]''.<ref name="Debrief">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story - The Official Mission Debrief]]''</ref> The adult [[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|novelization]] of ''Rogue One'' incorrectly states that Grek is the only pilot to crash into the Shield Gate<ref name="RON" /> even though a second vessel crashing is clearly visible in the film.<ref name="Rogue One" />

